{"name":"Hearts Afire","hex":"#d47a76","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hearts","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of heart"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of the four suits of playing cards, in red, marked with the symbol ♥.","A trick-taking card game in which players are penalized for taking hearts and (especially) the queen of spades."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hearts"},{"term":"afire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["On fire (often metaphorically)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["On fire (often metaphorically).","↑ Douglas Harper (2001–2026), “afire”, in Online Etymology Dictionary."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hearts Afire","blocks":[{"text":"Hearts Afire is an American television sitcom created by Linda Bloodworth-Thomason, starring John Ritter and Markie Post, that aired on CBS from September 14, 1992, to February 1, 1995. The series' title is taken from a line in the Earth, Wind & Fire song \"That's the Way of the World\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fc/Hearts_Afire_Cast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hearts_Afire","wikidata":"Q1797430"},{"title":"Afire","blocks":[{"text":"Afire is a 2023 German drama film directed by Christian Petzold, starring Thomas Schubert, Paula Beer, Langston Uibel and Enno Trebs. The relationship drama focuses on four people sharing a holiday home on the Baltic Sea."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/32/Afire_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afire","wikidata":"Q116621601"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Christian_Petzold_with_Silber_Bear%2C_Berlinale_2023.jpg/500px-Christian_Petzold_with_Silber_Bear%2C_Berlinale_